{
  "slug": "spiced-carrot-fritters-with-yoghurt-sauce",
  "title": "Spiced Carrot Fritters with Yoghurt Sauce",
  "blurb": "Golden carrot patties seasoned with cumin and cayenne, served with a cool garlic yoghurt dip.",
  "steps": [
    "Place the grated carrots in a clean tea towel and squeeze out as much liquid as possible, then transfer to a large bowl.",
    "Add the flour, eggs, cumin, cayenne, half the parsley, half the garlic and half the salt to the carrots and mix thoroughly until everything is combined.",
    "Heat half the olive oil in a large frying pan over medium heat.",
    "Shape heaped tablespoons of the mixture into patties and fry in batches for about 4 minutes each side until golden brown, adding more oil as needed.",
    "While the fritters cook, mix the yoghurt with the remaining garlic, lemon juice and remaining salt.",
    "Stir the remaining parsley into the yoghurt sauce and serve alongside the warm fritters."
  ],
